{"kind":"event","event_id":6935,"event_uid":"01M2NMCWEMMFCVDTXA26X461V9","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.metadata_updated","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":298,"issue_uid":"01M2NMBKZXQ77J2J33T01SM5JM","issue_short_id":"m5jm","actor":"impl:1@run-163","hlc_physical_ms":1789579915732,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"40c55e4626bcffbc5e91243cdd0b14d55cc7733557ba174f36ae66f1ff849988","payload":{"diff":{"work.attention":{"from":null,"to":"ok"}},"revision_new":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T17:31:55.731Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:31:55.732Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":6945,"event_uid":"01M2NME6FDCV8TH5T558RP43DE","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":298,"issue_uid":"01M2NMBKZXQ77J2J33T01SM5JM","issue_short_id":"m5jm","actor":"impl:1@run-163","hlc_physical_ms":1789579958765,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"21f94ba5ab0242acb1833a837c5ed1b3fa71ee5839c67ad58c30a593f1fd4012","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NME6FCXKR2EQ8Q1P5RGRR8","author":"impl:1@run-163","body":"Approach: the re-edge filter in `blockingSiblingsOf` reads the LIVE `adoptedIds`, which is why a sibling adopted after this task's dispatch head was read reads as 'already in the tree' and the BLOCKED fails instead of re-edging. Plan: add `adoptedAtDispatch` (Map task id -> Set), snapshotted with `new Set(adoptedIds)` in the same synchronous statement group as `const head = adoptedHead` at both dispatch sites (`dispatchOnce`, `retryParkedInfra`) — before `inFlight += 1` and before any await, because `foldEpoch` assigns `adoptedHead` and grows `adoptedIds` on adjacent lines from another lane. The filter then reads that snapshot (falling back to the live set when absent). `siblingsNow` and the two `waitingOn` sites keep reading the live set. Plus CONTRACT.md line 698: 'not yet adopted' -> 'not adopted in the head the task's dispatch went out on'. The guarded exam at fleet/tests/test_run_engine_re_edge.mjs is the peer's; I verify the new (d.5) shape with a scratch copy outside the tree and leave the guarded path untouched.","created_at":"2026-09-16T17:32:38.764914488Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T17:32:38.765Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":6957,"event_uid":"01M2NMP2EQ62M4G40J3KC8NB8N","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":298,"issue_uid":"01M2NMBKZXQ77J2J33T01SM5JM","issue_short_id":"m5jm","actor":"impl:1@run-163","hlc_physical_ms":1789580216791,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"32d67bd3fba16fdf408d7cf65fde6f581e35ea1aabdbbdc5e1c539d036f9a19c","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2NMP2EP68JGMD62S6B1T5EB","author":"impl:1@run-163","body":"Done at 8e667644. `adoptedAtDispatch` (Map id -> Set) is snapshotted with `new Set(adoptedIds)` in the same synchronous statement group as `const head = adoptedHead` at both dispatch sites (dispatchOnce, retryParkedInfra), before `inFlight += 1` and before the first await; `blockingSiblingsOf` filters on that snapshot with a live-set fallback no dispatch can reach. siblingsNow, the two waitingOn sites and the one-re-edge-per-pair cap are untouched. CONTRACT.md's re-edge bullet now reads 'not adopted in the head this task's dispatch went out on'.\n\nVerification, since the guarded exam at fleet/tests/test_run_engine_re_edge.mjs is the peer's and I left it untouched: I built the (d.5) shape in a scratch copy at fleet/tests/_scratch_d5.mjs (deleted before commit, not in the diff) — A and B, no plan edge, width 2, foldAgeMs: 0, B's first implementer holding until a driver:wave-adopted naming A is on the log, then filing blocks A->B and returning BLOCKED; plus the M2 counterpart with a plan edge A->B. Both legs pass with the change. Against the BASE engine the (d.5a) leg is red with 0 !== 1 driver:re-edged and the log '… driver:wave-adopted [\"A\"] | driver:integrated-clean | worker:start impl:B | worker:end impl:B' — B's dispatch read the head before A was adopted and A landed during anchorClone, which is exactly the race. All 17 fleet/tests/test_run_engine_*.mjs suites and the hermetic probe are green.","cre